--- body ---
## Context

Protocol_05 §3.4 (pre-registered revision (d)) bans Wikipedia / Wikidata /
DBpedia / mirrors / aggregator re-syndication as Source 1 or Source 2,
because a derivative of the reference dataset was published on Wikipedia
before the experiment. The protocol states: "Compliance is auditable:
Phase D synthesis counts Wikipedia/Wikidata citations in each output's
bibliography. Zero is compliant."

`slides/manuscript/main.md` (the arXiv preprint) discloses the
contamination risk but never answers the reader's next question: *did the
ban hold?* Author decision 2026-06-06: the compliance COUNT goes into
Annex C. It is a descriptive disclosure (a count, not an inferential
test), so it amends — not violates — ticket 0433's "no statistics in
Annex C" invariant. The full pre-registered H5 treatment (Wilson upper
bounds per agent) stays deferred to the report.tex chapter (ticket 0259).

## Scope

Three deliverables: script, macro, prose.

1. **Script** `src/aedist/audit_exp2_wiki_citations.py` (argparse,
   logging, no hardcoded paths — defaults from the same conventions as
   `src/aedist/extract_exp2_bib.py`, which already parses these files and
   whose helpers should be reused). Scan the 40 registered runs in
   `experiments/derived/arm1_flat/` (naive) and `arm2_flat/` (optimised):
   inventory Source 1 / Source 2 cells AND bibliography entries. Count
   citations whose URL/domain matches the banned set from protocol_05
   §3.4: `*.wikipedia.org` (any language subdomain, incl. `*.m.*`
   mirrors), `wikidata.org`, `dbpedia.org`, plus an explicit short list of
   known Wikipedia mirrors. Mechanical domain matching only; do NOT
   attempt LLM judgement of "aggregator re-syndication" — out of scope,
   note it as a limitation. Output: per-run CSV
   `report/inputs/generated/tab_exp2_wiki_compliance.csv`
   (agent, arm, run, n_cells_s1s2, n_banned_s1s2, n_bib_entries,
   n_banned_bib).

2. **Macro**: emit the aggregate values (total banned-citation count per
   arm, n runs scanned) as `\newcommand` macros for report/slides reuse.
   Per `.claude/rules/writing.md`: ≤3 new values → append to the existing
   generated macros file (e.g. `macros_slides.tex` generator), do NOT
   create a new `\InputIfFileExists` include (tectonic bundle trap).
   NOTE: `main.md` builds via pandoc and inputs no macro file — the prose
   quotes the literal number; guard it with an adherence/consistency test
   asserting the literal in main.md matches the generated CSV (pattern of
   ratchet ticket 0447).

3. **Prose**: one or two sentences in Annex C of
   `slides/manuscript/main.md` (l.256–339), adjacent to the existing
   leakage/contamination discussion. Report the count per arm. Phrasing
   discipline: if zero in the optimised arm, write "we did not detect any
   banned-domain citation across the N parsable optimised-arm outputs" —
   never "there are none" (protocol_05 reporting rule + writing.md
   epistemic humility). Naive-arm counts are NOT violations — the naive
   prompt (Doc-07) carries no source taxonomy; report them as unaided
   baseline behaviour, the contrast being itself informative.

## Makefile DAG

Wire the script into `experiments/render.mk` (P3 render workpackage) as
its own one-output-per-rule target; prerequisites must match the script's
actual reads (`arm1_flat`, `arm2_flat`) and writes. No P3-to-P3
side-output edges (ticket 0436 rule). Commit the generated CSV/macros
(handoff artifacts — never gitignored).

## First test

`tests/test_audit_exp2_wiki_citations.py`: feed a synthetic run markdown
containing (a) an inventory row citing `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X`
in Source 1, (b) a bibliography entry citing
`https://vi.m.wikipedia.org/...`, (c) a clean row citing `moit.gov.vn`.
Assert counts: n_banned_s1s2 == 1, n_banned_bib == 1, clean row not
counted. Plus the main.md literal-consistency adherence test.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Script counts banned-domain citations per run across the 40
      registered runs; CSV + macro artifacts generated and committed
- [x] `experiments/render.mk` target added; DAG prerequisites match the
      script's actual reads/writes
- [x] Annex C sentence(s) report the per-arm count with "we did not
      detect" phrasing for any zero; consistency test guards the quoted
      literal against the CSV
- [x] Unit tests for the domain matcher; `make check` passes

## Imagine verdict (raid 2026-06-06) — binding refinements

- **Approach**: standalone P3 script importing parsing helpers from
  `extract_exp2_bib` (`_parse_table_rows`, `_find_source_columns`,
  `_find_bib_section`, `_RUN_RE`). Do NOT extend the P2 script (CSV
  schema blast radius: `_FIELDS`, tabulator `_load_rows`, mart views).
- **Inputs**: `experiments/derived/arm1_flat/` + `arm2_flat/` (canonical
  P3 inputs; precedent `tabulate_exp2_2x2.py`, render.mk ~l.216).
  Bibliography source of truth = the main `<agent>_runNN.md` via
  `_find_bib_section`; some `_bib.md` sidecars are 1 byte.
- **Macro mechanism**: emit `macros_wiki_compliance.tex` as a grouped
  `&:` co-output of the audit rule (precedent render.mk l.236/431/455).
  Do NOT append to `macros_slides.tex` (different input tree —
  forbidden P3-to-P3 coupling, ticket 0436). No document \inputs it yet;
  consumer is deferred 0259.
- **Banned set** (suffix match `host == d or host.endswith("." + d)`):
  frozenset {wikipedia.org, wikidata.org, dbpedia.org, wikiwand.com}.
  Covers language + m-dot subdomains. NEAR-MISS: `gem.wiki` (Global
  Energy Monitor) is an ALLOWED secondary source — suffix rule excludes
  it; add an explicit regression test.
- **Scan only** Source 1 / Source 2 cells and bibliography entries.
  NEVER Notes/prose — Notes contain compliance signals like
  "Lead: Wikipedia (inadmissible)" that are the OPPOSITE of violations.
- **DATA FINDING (changes the prose; CORRECTED by feasibility pass)**:
  the ban did NOT fully hold, in TWO agents. Mistral optimised arm:
  runs 01-04 cite `en.wikipedia.org` (S1/S2 and/or bibliography),
  run05 clean. OpenAI optimised arm: run01 cites `en.wikipedia.org` in
  a Source 2 cell (`arm2_flat/openai_run01.md` l.30). Anthropic and
  Qwen arm2 are clean. Naive arm baseline: OpenAI run05 cites Wikipedia
  in Source 2. Per protocol §3.4 non-zero is reported as a
  protocol-compliance violation alongside F1. "We did not detect"
  phrasing applies ONLY per agent×arm cells that are genuinely zero.
  No blanket compliance claim. PROSE MUST BE DERIVED FROM THE GENERATED
  CSV, not from this enumeration.

## Plan (raid 2026-06-06) — verified against source

1. `src/aedist/audit_exp2_wiki_citations.py`: import `_parse_table_rows`
   (l.171), `_find_source_columns` (l.157), `_find_bib_section` (l.219),
   `_RUN_RE` (l.27) from `extract_exp2_bib` (module-level; ruff has no
   PLC2701; precedent: tests import `_FIELDS`). `BANNED_DOMAINS`
   frozenset {wikipedia.org, wikidata.org, dbpedia.org, wikiwand.com};
   `is_banned_domain(url)` = urlparse + suffix match; `audit_run(path)`
   counts banned URLs in Source 1/2 cells (NOT Notes) + bibliography
   section; `audit_all(naive_dir, optimised_dir)` → 40 rows. CLI:
   `--naive-dir` (default arm1_flat), `--optimised-dir` (arm2_flat),
   `--output` CSV, `--output-macros` .tex. Logging, not print.
2. CSV `report/inputs/generated/tab_exp2_wiki_compliance.csv`
   (agent,arm,run,n_cells_s1s2,n_banned_s1s2,n_bib_entries,n_banned_bib);
   macros `macros_wiki_compliance.tex`: \ExpTwoWikiRunsScanned,
   \ExpTwoWikiBannedOptimised, \ExpTwoWikiBannedNaive,
   \ExpTwoWikiBannedTotal (CamelCase no-digit convention, cf.
   macros_exp1_matrix.tex). Banned{Arm} = runs with any banned cite.
3. render.mk: grouped `&:` rule (precedent l.236/358/431/455), prereqs =
   `$(wildcard $(ANALYSIS_DERIVED_DIR)/arm{1,2}_flat/*.md)` + script;
   no .done stamps (score.mk artifacts). Add CSV to report-tables list.
4. Tests `tests/test_audit_exp2_wiki_citations.py` (imitate
   test_extract_exp2_bib.py): unit is_banned_domain (en/vi.m wikipedia
   TRUE, wikidata TRUE, wikiwand TRUE, dbpedia TRUE, gem.wiki FALSE,
   moit.gov.vn FALSE, bare word FALSE); synthetic 3-row fixture →
   n_banned_s1s2 == 2 exactly (Notes with "Wikipedia" text must NOT
   inflate — catches column-index bugs), n_banned_bib == 1; integration
   (marked): mistral arm2 run02 n_banned_s1s2 > 0 (pins finding),
   anthropic optimised total == 0 (pins Notes exclusion), 40 rows;
   adherence: independent regex over main.md literal vs CSV aggregate
   (no import of script formatting — anti-tautology).
5. ORDER (test-one-before-blasting): script+unit tests → run on real
   data → INSPECT CSV → prose with actual numbers → consistency test →
   make check. Expected from grep: Mistral arm2 runs 01-04 banned >0,
   run05 = 0; OpenAI arm1 run05 S2 wikipedia; others zero in S1/S2.
6. Prose: insert after "What this experiment does and does not test"
   paragraph (main.md ~l.339, before ---): ban rationale (1 sentence,
   reference-derivative-on-Wikipedia disclosure), audit method
   (mechanical URL-domain match, 40 runs), optimised-arm finding
   ("we detected ... in N of the 20 optimised-arm runs, concentrated in
   Mistral; the remaining three agents' optimised runs contained no
   banned-domain citation"), naive-arm count as unaided baseline (no ban
   applied there), mechanical-matching limitation sentence.

## Feasibility (raid 2026-06-06) — verdict PASS after corrections

Verified: paths.mk vars `ANALYSIS_GEN` (l.27) / `ANALYSIS_DERIVED_DIR`
(l.29) / `ANALYSIS_REPO_ROOT` (l.23); invocation `uv run python -m
aedist.X` + `@mkdir -p $(dir $@)` (exemplar render.mk l.216-222);
`&:` precedents l.236/358/431/455; 20+20 run files; pyproject
`packages = ["src/aedist"]`; markers integration/adherence defined;
no conflicting commits or claims (0433 open, unclaimed).

Binding corrections for the executor:
1. **OpenAI arm2 run01 violates too** (S2 cell, l.30) — integration
   tests must pin `mistral arm2 > 0`, `openai arm2 run01 > 0`,
   `anthropic arm2 == 0`, `qwen arm2 == 0`. Prose names BOTH agents.
2. **Make wildcard has no brace expansion**: two separate
   `$(wildcard .../arm1_flat/*.md)` `$(wildcard .../arm2_flat/*.md)`
   prerequisites.
3. `_find_source_columns` returns dict with `src1`, `src2`, AND
   `notes` keys — iterate ONLY src1/src2.
4. main.md anchor: the heading "What this experiment does and does not
   test" occurs TWICE (l.252 §4 body, l.337 Annex C) — insert after the
   SECOND, before the `---` at l.341.
5. Consistency-test regex must not collide with the existing l.133
   "CACM Wikidata-overview DOI" mention — anchor the regex on the
   compliance sentence's own wording (e.g. "of the 20 optimised-arm
   runs"), and keep that wording in the prose.
6. `_RUN_RE` is at l.26 (not 27). Wire the macros .tex co-output (or
   the CSV var) into `report-tables` (l.390) or `exp2-analysis-report`
   (l.254) — follow how `$(ANALYSIS_EXP2_2X2_TEX)` is listed (l.395).

